---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base wide pageClass="quiet-index-page" title="Colophon" description="Technical, editorial, accessibility, and privacy notes for Ian Helfrich's website.">
  <div class="quiet-shell">
    <header class="quiet-header">
      <div><p class="quiet-label">Site record · August 2026</p><h1>How this site is built</h1></div>
      <p class="quiet-lead">The website is a static public record built with Astro. Its design separates plain-language context, technical detail, artifact links, and limits.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="colophon-section" aria-labelledby="colophon-publishing">
      <p class="section-label">Publishing</p>
      <h2 id="colophon-publishing">A static site with dated records</h2>
      <div class="two-registers">
        <p>Research, dataset, project, and writing records are generated from versioned content files. Pagefind creates a static browser-search index during deployment. GitHub Pages serves the finished files.</p>
        <aside><strong>Public boundary</strong><span>Only records cleared for public discovery enter the index, sitemap, RSS feed, and generated research routes.</span></aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="colophon-section" aria-labelledby="colophon-design">
      <p class="section-label">Design and type</p>
      <h2 id="colophon-design">One visual system across the record</h2>
      <div class="two-registers">
        <p>Geist structures headings and navigation, Newsreader carries longer explanations, and Geist Mono labels status, dates, methods, and controls. All three fonts are served locally. The palette uses mineral paper, white figures, dark ink, and three functional signal colors.</p>
        <aside><strong>Motion rule</strong><span>Motion responds to navigation, focus, hover, or a direct calculation. Reduced-motion preferences remove nonessential transitions.</span></aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="colophon-section" aria-labelledby="colophon-interactions">
      <p class="section-label">Calculations</p>
      <h2 id="colophon-interactions">Demonstrations stay with their evidence</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Interactive figures are used where changing an input clarifies a model, comparison, or teaching idea. Their numerical meaning, status, and limit remain available in HTML outside the graphic.</p>
      <ul class="link-list">
        <li><a href="/research/helfrich-2026-nmtc-rural-gap#cde-decomposition">NMTC coefficient decomposition</a><span>Descriptive place-based-policy comparison</span></li>
        <li><a href="/research/helfrich-2024-ssrn-4772016#optimal-transport">Optimal-transport calculation</a><span>Finite-grid teaching and research demonstration</span></li>
        <li><a href="/projects/applied-statistics#least-squares-lab">Least-squares sensitivity lab</a><span>Editable statistics teaching fixture</span></li>
        <li><a href="/teaching#representation-relay">Representation relay</a><span>One relationship shown in several forms</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="colophon-section" aria-labelledby="colophon-privacy">
      <p class="section-label">Privacy and access</p>
      <h2 id="colophon-privacy">No learner or client record belongs here</h2>
      <div class="two-registers">
        <p>The public site does not identify tutoring clients, coaching participants, or private advisory relationships. Archival teaching builds that remain reachable by an older direct link are excluded from search and marked noindex.</p>
        <aside><strong>Source</strong><a href="https://github.com/ihelfrich/ihelfrich.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View the site repository</a></aside>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .quiet-shell { width: min(100%, 72rem); margin-inline: auto; }
  .quiet-header { display: grid; padding-block: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem); grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(18rem, .7fr); gap: 2rem 5rem; align-items: end; border-block: 1px solid var(--ef-ink); }
  .quiet-label, .section-label, .two-registers aside strong { color: var(--muted); font: 620 .68rem/1.5 var(--font-data); letter-spacing: .07em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1 { max-width: 11ch; margin: .6rem 0 0; font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 8vw, 7rem); }
  .quiet-lead { margin: 0; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .colophon-section { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ef-ink); }
  .colophon-section h2 { max-width: 18ch; margin: .45rem 0 2rem; font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  .two-registers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(15rem, 20rem); gap: 2rem 5rem; }
  .two-registers > p, .section-intro { max-width: 66ch; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .two-registers aside { display: grid; align-content: start; gap: .4rem; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--ef-signal); }
  .two-registers aside a { display: inline-flex; min-height: 44px; align-items: center; }
  .link-list { margin: 2rem 0 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--ef-ink); list-style: none; }
  .link-list li { display: grid; margin: 0; padding-block: 1rem; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(14rem, 22rem); gap: 1rem 3rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .link-list a { color: var(--ef-ink); font: 600 1.1rem/1.4 var(--font-display); }
  .link-list span { color: var(--muted); }
  @media (max-width: 45rem) { .quiet-header, .two-registers, .link-list li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
